//! The rules ledger: every Syntax Rule restriction ("shall") and every
//! condition a General or Syntax Rule raises, in Clauses 6 to 23. Each entry says
//! which row of the matrix it belongs to and how it is held:
//!
//! - [`Coverage::Test`]: a test in `gql_conformance.rs` pins it (`probe`:
//!   the row's own probe and expected result do).
//! - [`Coverage::Extension`]: the rule restricts what conforming GQL may
//!   say, and the engine also accepts text that breaks it, with Cypher's
//!   meaning. §5.3.2.3 leaves the treatment of non-conforming language
//!   implementation-defined (IE005), so a conforming query is unaffected.
//! - [`Coverage::Deviation`]: a conforming query gets an answer other than
//!   the books' (§24.5.3), kept for Cypher. `query-language/gql/deviations.md` lists these.
//! - [`Coverage::NotApplicable`]: it cannot arise here, because it concerns
//!   an optional feature, or an implementation-defined choice rules it out.
//! - [`Coverage::Gap`]: it should hold and does not yet.
//! - [`Coverage::Pending`]: its feature does not run yet. Whoever implements
//!   the feature pins it; the test fails once the feature runs while any of
//!   its rules is still pending.
//!
//! The entries were read from the books: each Syntax Rule that restricts what
//! a query may say and each rule that raises a condition, in every subclause
//! of Clauses 6 to 23, as Technical Corrigendum 1:2026 amends them, described
//! here in our own words. Rules of a feature that does not run are grouped
//! by subclause. The test
//! checks that every named test exists and every row is a row of the matrix,
//! and it derives each running row's Diagnostics cell from these entries.

/// How a rule is held.
pub enum Coverage {
    Test(&'static str),
    Extension(&'static str),
    Deviation(&'static str),
    NotApplicable(&'static str),
    Gap(&'static str),
    Pending(&'static str),
}

/// One rule of the books.
pub struct Rule {
    /// Subclause and rule, as `§20.22 GR 7`; `(Cor 1)` where the corrigendum
    /// replaces it.
    pub at: &'static str,
    /// The `FEATURES` row the rule belongs to.
    pub row: &'static str,
    /// What the rule requires, in our words, with the GQLSTATUS it raises.
    pub what: &'static str,
    pub coverage: Coverage,
}

